<bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_22"><bpmn:participant id="Participant_22" name="BPMN-22 | Courier Address Eligibility and Delivery Fee Quotation" processRef="Process_22_Reference"/><bpmn:participant id="Provider_22_Maps" name="Google Maps Platform"/><bpmn:participant id="Provider_22_Lalamove" name="Lalamove ? quotation only"/><bpmn:messageFlow id="M22_MapsRequest" sourceRef="N22_Maps" targetRef="Provider_22_Maps" name="Address validation / location request"/><bpmn:messageFlow id="M22_MapsResponse" sourceRef="Provider_22_Maps" targetRef="N22_Maps" name="Location result / provider issue"/><bpmn:messageFlow id="M22_QuoteRequest" sourceRef="N22_Quote" targetRef="Provider_22_Lalamove" name="Applicable quotation request(s)"/><bpmn:messageFlow id="M22_QuoteResponse" sourceRef="Provider_22_Lalamove" targetRef="N22_Quote" name="Fee quotation(s) / provider issue"/></bpmn:collaboration>
<bpmn:process id="Process_22_Reference" name="Courier Address Eligibility and Delivery Fee Quotation" isExecutable="false">
<bpmn:documentation>Sources: docs/proposed-bpmn-catalog.md, BPMN-22 and all catalog reuse rules; Chapters/Kitchen406 - Capstone Paper.md, SRS 4.4 FR-ADDR-04-05, 4.16 FR-DEL-02-09, BR-26-27. Implementation inspected: index.html and its app/checkout.js, address-map.js, address-state.js, delivery-route.js and subscription-checkout.js modules. Implementation uses sample area/fees; diagram follows the proposed SRS Maps and Lalamove behavior. Read top to bottom. Two responsibility lanes belong to the same Kitchen406 System; sequence flows remain in this pool and message flows connect black-box external providers. Service tasks encompass request/response evaluation, including provider failure/timeout; no unspecified timer duration is invented. BPMN-02 invokes this reusable process and handles selection, correction, retry and purchase review; BPMN-35 owns saved address maintenance; BPMN-19 owns later courier booking. No nested call is necessary. Process ID matches the existing BPMN-02 calledElement Process_22_Reference in the same target namespace. Separate files are descriptive cross-references, not a packaged executable deployment. No existing diagram needs modification.</bpmn:documentation>
<bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_22"><bpmn:lane id="Lane_22_Checkout" name="Kitchen406 System ? Checkout coordination"><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_Start</bpmn:flowNodeRef><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_Input</bpmn:flowNodeRef><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_MapIssue</bpmn:flowNodeRef><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_MapEnd</bpmn:flowNodeRef><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_Outside</bpmn:flowNodeRef><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_OutsideEnd</bpmn:flowNodeRef><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_QuoteIssue</bpmn:flowNodeRef><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_QuoteEnd</bpmn:flowNodeRef></bpmn:lane><bpmn:lane id="Lane_22_Delivery" name="Kitchen406 System ? Delivery validation and quotation"><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_Maps</bpmn:flowNodeRef><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_Located</bpmn:flowNodeRef><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_Area</bpmn:flowNodeRef><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_Eligible</bpmn:flowNodeRef><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_Quote</bpmn:flowNodeRef><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_Usable</bpmn:flowNodeRef><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_Result</bpmn:flowNodeRef><bpmn:flowNodeRef>N22_Done</bpmn:flowNodeRef></bpmn:lane></bpmn:laneSet>
<bpmn:startEvent id="N22_Start" name="Delivery check requested by BPMN-02"><bpmn:documentation>Input: authenticated customer, selected saved address, purchase type, bakery origin and applicable delivery schedule(s). Only standard orders and courier subscriptions enter this process. Pickup bypasses it; custom cakes use BPMN-08 and BPMN-21.</bpmn:documentation><bpmn:outgoing>F22_01</bpmn:outgoing></bpmn:startEvent>
<bpmn:serviceTask id="N22_Input" name="Load selected address and applicable delivery schedules"><bpmn:documentation>FR-ADDR-05; FR-DEL-02. Use the address selected in BPMN-02. One destination applies to all four subscription fulfillments (BR-26). Address-book editing belongs to BPMN-35; do not repeat it here.</bpmn:documentation><bpmn:incoming>F22_01</bpmn:incoming><bpmn:outgoing>F22_02</bpmn:outgoing></bpmn:serviceTask>
<bpmn:serviceTask id="N22_Maps" name="Validate and locate selected address with Google Maps"><bpmn:documentation>FR-ADDR-04; FR-DEL-03. Request validation/location and evaluate the response. Missing or invalid address, unresolved location, unavailable provider or timeout returns an address/provider issue; no eligibility is inferred from the prototype city list.</bpmn:documentation><bpmn:incoming>F22_02</bpmn:incoming><bpmn:outgoing>F22_03</bpmn:outgoing></bpmn:serviceTask>
<bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="N22_Located" name="Valid location returned?"><bpmn:incoming>F22_03</bpmn:incoming><bpmn:outgoing>F22_04</bpmn:outgoing><bpmn:outgoing>F22_06</bpmn:outgoing></bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
<bpmn:serviceTask id="N22_MapIssue" name="Return address / Maps issue; block delivery checkout"><bpmn:documentation>Return a correction/retry reason to BPMN-02. No fee is accepted; unavailable service is not an outside-area determination. BPMN-02 owns customer recovery.</bpmn:documentation><bpmn:incoming>F22_04</bpmn:incoming><bpmn:outgoing>F22_05</bpmn:outgoing></bpmn:serviceTask>
<bpmn:endEvent id="N22_MapEnd" name="Address check unsuccessful ? return to BPMN-02"><bpmn:incoming>F22_05</bpmn:incoming></bpmn:endEvent>
<bpmn:businessRuleTask id="N22_Area" name="Check configured courier service area (default maximum 10 km)"><bpmn:documentation>FR-DEL-04. Evaluate the located destination relative to the bakery using configured service-area rules. The SRS does not prescribe a distance algorithm; do not substitute the prototype city whitelist as the proposed policy.</bpmn:documentation><bpmn:incoming>F22_06</bpmn:incoming><bpmn:outgoing>F22_07</bpmn:outgoing></bpmn:businessRuleTask>
<bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="N22_Eligible" name="Within supported service area?"><bpmn:incoming>F22_07</bpmn:incoming><bpmn:outgoing>F22_08</bpmn:outgoing><bpmn:outgoing>F22_10</bpmn:outgoing></bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
<bpmn:serviceTask id="N22_Outside" name="Return outside-area result; block delivery checkout"><bpmn:documentation>FR-DEL-05. No Lalamove fee request for an ineligible destination. BPMN-02 offers address correction, another arrangement or leaving.</bpmn:documentation><bpmn:incoming>F22_08</bpmn:incoming><bpmn:outgoing>F22_09</bpmn:outgoing></bpmn:serviceTask>
<bpmn:endEvent id="N22_OutsideEnd" name="Ineligible address ? return to BPMN-02"><bpmn:incoming>F22_09</bpmn:incoming></bpmn:endEvent>
<bpmn:serviceTask id="N22_Quote" name="Request applicable delivery fee quotation(s) from Lalamove"><bpmn:documentation>FR-DEL-06, 09. Send bakery origin, validated destination and applicable delivery context. Standard order: applicable delivery fee. Subscription: cover all four scheduled fulfillments and return the per-fulfillment fees and combined prepaid delivery amount (BR-27). This task represents quotation requests only; no booking is created.</bpmn:documentation><bpmn:incoming>F22_10</bpmn:incoming><bpmn:outgoing>F22_11</bpmn:outgoing></bpmn:serviceTask>
<bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="N22_Usable" name="All required fees available?"><bpmn:incoming>F22_11</bpmn:incoming><bpmn:outgoing>F22_12</bpmn:outgoing><bpmn:outgoing>F22_14</bpmn:outgoing></bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
<bpmn:serviceTask id="N22_QuoteIssue" name="Return quotation failure; block delivery checkout"><bpmn:documentation>Return missing, unusable, failed or unavailable quotation outcome, including provider timeout. Partial subscription quotations do not enable checkout. Do not replace missing fees with zero or a sample fee. Retry is controlled by BPMN-02, without an invented automatic retry schedule.</bpmn:documentation><bpmn:incoming>F22_12</bpmn:incoming><bpmn:outgoing>F22_13</bpmn:outgoing></bpmn:serviceTask>
<bpmn:endEvent id="N22_QuoteEnd" name="Quotation unavailable ? return to BPMN-02"><bpmn:incoming>F22_13</bpmn:incoming></bpmn:endEvent>
<bpmn:serviceTask id="N22_Result" name="Return eligible destination and fee breakdown to BPMN-02"><bpmn:documentation>FR-DEL-07-08. Return selected address/location, eligibility and applicable provider quotation information and amounts, including all four subscription fees. BPMN-02 displays fees in the purchase summary before payment and hands reviewed details onward. Preserve confirmed-order delivery data through BPMN-09/13 for subsequent BPMN-19 booking. No reservation, payment or order confirmation occurs here.</bpmn:documentation><bpmn:incoming>F22_14</bpmn:incoming><bpmn:outgoing>F22_15</bpmn:outgoing></bpmn:serviceTask>
<bpmn:endEvent id="N22_Done" name="Eligible address and quotation(s) returned"><bpmn:incoming>F22_15</bpmn:incoming></bpmn:endEvent>
